      {
        "question_text": "(a) Buy $375$ shares at $\\$8.62$ each with a flat brokerage fee of $\\$31$. Find the total cost.\n(b) Sell $640$ shares at $\\$5.47$ each with a flat brokerage fee of $\\$29$. Find the total income.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Share cost $=375\\times8.62=\\$3232.50$.\nTotal cost $=3232.50+31=\\$3263.50$.\n(b) Share income $=640\\times5.47=\\$3500.80$.\nTotal income $=3500.80-29=\\$3471.80$.\nAdd the fee when buying; subtract it when selling."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Buy $725$ shares at $\\$6.84$ each with $1.4\\%$ brokerage.\n(b) Sell $920$ shares at $\\$7.36$ each with $1.8\\%$ brokerage.\nFind the total cost in (a) and total income in (b), to the nearest cent.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Share cost $=725\\times6.84=\\$4959$.\nBrokerage $=0.014\\times4959=\\$69.426$.\nTotal cost $=4959+69.426\\approx\\$5028.43$.\n(b) Share income $=920\\times7.36=\\$6771.20$.\nBrokerage $=0.018\\times6771.20=\\$121.8816$.\nTotal income $=6771.20-121.8816\\approx\\$6649.32$.\nKeep the original values until rounding the final amount."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Alex bought $240$ shares for $\\$18.50$ each and later sold them for $\\$23.20$ each. Brokerage fees for buying and selling totalled $\\$54$.\nWhat was the profit?",
        "solution_text": "Share cost $=240\\times18.50=\\$4440$.\nShare income $=240\\times23.20=\\$5568$.\nProfit:\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}5568-4440-54\\\\&=\\$1074\\end{aligned}$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Sam bought $350$ shares for $\\$16.80$ each and later sold them for $\\$20.40$ each. Brokerage fees for buying and selling totalled $\\$63$.\n(a) What was the profit?\n(b) What was the profit as a percentage of the cost of the shares before brokerage? Answer to two decimal places.",
        "solution_text": "Share cost $=350\\times16.80=\\$5880$.\nShare income $=350\\times20.40=\\$7140$.\n(a) Profit:\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}7140-5880-63\\\\&=\\$1197\\end{aligned}$\n(b) Percentage profit:\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{1197}{5880}\\times100\\%\\\\&\\approx20.36\\%\\end{aligned}$"
      }
    ],
